# PROVENANCE: the shape the grok CLI was VERIFIED to write on 2026-08-20 (commit
# 57c8bd7, read off live hub session ledgers): the usage dict is NOT at the top
# level, it rides nested inside params.update, and it carries inputTokens,
# outputTokens, cachedReadTokens, cacheCreationTokens and costUsdTicks
# (1e-10 USD, so 9056360000 ticks = $0.905636). The KEY NAMES and the NESTING
# are from that verification. The surrounding envelope fields (jsonrpc, method,
# sessionUpdate) are illustrative padding, and the parser must not depend on any
# of them — that dependency is the bug this fixture exists to pin.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"s-406","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"working on it"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"s-406","update":{"sessionUpdate":"usage","usage":{"inputTokens":120000,"outputTokens":3100,"cachedReadTokens":41000,"cacheCreationTokens":900,"costUsdTicks":3011000000}}}}
